1. TDLib (Telegram Database Library) -- Boost Software License 1.0 (BSL-1.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Copyright Aliaksei Levin (levlam@telegram.org),
Arseny Smirnov (arseny30@gmail.com) 2014-2026
https://github.com/tdlib/td

Bundled as:
  - app/src/main/java/org/drinkless/tdlib/Client.java
  - app/src/main/java/org/drinkless/tdlib/TdApi.java
  - app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/libtdjni.so
  - app/src/main/jniLibs/x86_64/libtdjni.so

License: https://www.boost.org/LICENSE_1_0.txt

Binary provenance (libtdjni.so):
  The native libraries are built by the manually dispatched GitHub Actions
  workflow .github/workflows/build-tdlib.yml. It clones
  https://github.com/tdlib/td, checks out commit 8921c22f0f85 (the workflow's
  default `td_ref` input), and runs TDLib's own example/android scripts
  (fetch-sdk.sh, build-openssl.sh, build-tdlib.sh), patched to build only the
  arm64-v8a and x86_64 ABIs. The workflow uploads a tdlib.zip artifact; its
  libs/<abi>/libtdjni.so files and Java sources were copied by hand into the
  paths above. To reproduce: run the workflow with the same td_ref and
  vendor the output.

